>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. The six-membered arene is a neutral ligand. The other fragment retains one NH₂ and an epoxide oxygen spanning two adjacent carbons, Electronic structure indicates bonding along all three edges of the three-membered ring. Assign a neutral epoxydienamine, two Cl⁻ and Ru(II). Localized 6 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

